course: dictionary
lesson: 1830
title: Coastline: where land meets sea
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A coastline is the edge of the land where it meets the sea. It can mean the whole edge, or the shape of that edge as you see it on a map or along a long stretch of coast.
explain: Read the words around it. «From the late 1200s, sailors in the Mediterranean used portolan charts, sea maps with coastlines and criss-crossing compass lines.» Sea maps have coastlines on them, so a coastline is part of the land drawn on a map.
explain: Coastlines are not always the same. Waves wear away cliffs, and sand builds up into beaches. Try the swap check: in «confusing coastlines», the words «confusing the edge of the land where it meets the sea» still make sense.
fact: A coastline is the edge of the land where it meets the sea.
fact: «Coastlines and rivers have changed since 1337» shows that coastlines can change over time.
fact: Erosion is when waves wear away cliffs, and deposition is when sand builds up, such as a beach.
fact: Features of a coastline include bays, headlands, cliffs, stacks and spits.
fact: In maths, the coastline paradox says the more carefully you measure a coastline, the longer it seems.
exercise: What is a coastline? | A rope used to tie a boat | A deep part of the ocean floor | *The edge of the land where it meets the sea | A type of compass
exercise: Which of these is a feature you might find along a coastline? | Mountain peak | *Headland | Glacier | Desert dune
exercise: In maths, the more carefully you measure a coastline, the ___ it seems. | louder | colder | shorter | *longer
test: Sand piling up to build a beach is called what? | Stranding | *Deposition | Reclaiming | Erosion
test: According to the text, why might a whale strand on a beach? | Because it wants to eat sand | Because it loves sunshine | Because it is too small | *Because of sickness or confusing coastlines
exam: What does the word coastline mean? | A line of boats out on the water | *The edge of the land where it meets the sea | A stripe painted on the ocean | A rope tied to a ship
